  "body_html": "<h1>Knapsack Auction Environment</h1>\n<p>A knapsack auction is a single-parameter mechanism equipped with public item\nweights and a total capacity constraint.</p>\n<p>The interface records the public item sizes, the capacity, weight and capacity\nsign assumptions, feasibility, and capacity-respecting allocation rules.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[AGT, Chapter 12, Section 12.2] Nisan, Roughgarden, Tardos, and Vazirani,\n  <em>Algorithmic Game Theory</em>, <code>references/AlgorithmicGameTheory.pdf</code>.\n  Single-parameter domains and monotone allocation rules for truthful\n  approximation mechanisms.</li>\n<li>[AGT, Chapter 11, Sections 11.1-11.2] Nisan, Roughgarden, Tardos, and\n  Vazirani, <em>Algorithmic Game Theory</em>, <code>references/AlgorithmicGameTheory.pdf</code>.\n  Combinatorial-auction allocation constraints and single-minded bidder\n  feasibility models.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Provenance</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrated from EconCSLib pull request 27, old blueprint label\n  <code>def:auction_knapsack_environment</code> in <code>blueprint/src/content.tex</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
